      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The average cost to reroof a house in Utah ranges from $8,000 to $20,000, with most homeowners paying between $10,500 and $19,500 for a standard asphalt shingle roof replacement.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "$8,000 to $20,000"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Cost by Roofing Material"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Prices vary significantly depending on the material you select for Utah\u2019s climate, which features hot summers and heavy winter snow:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Asphalt Shingles: $4.50 \u2013 $8.25 per sq. ft. (Estimated $9,000 \u2013 $16,500 for a 2,000 sq. ft. home)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roofing: $8.00 \u2013 $17.00 per sq. ft. (Estimated $16,000 \u2013 $34,000 for a 2,000 sq. ft. home)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Tile Roofing: $10.00 \u2013 $15.00 per sq. ft."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Designer or Premium Shingles: $9.00 \u2013 $18.00 per sq. ft. (Estimated $18,000 \u2013 $36,000 for a 2,000 sq. ft. home)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Factors That Change the Price"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Size and Pitch: Roofers measure by \"squares\" (one square equals 100 square feet). Steeper slopes or complex angles require extra safety gear and more labor, increasing costs by 10% to 20%."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Tear-off and Disposal: Removing old, multiple layers of roofing adds labor and disposal fees."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Decking Repairs: If rotten or damaged plywood sheathing is found underneath the old shingles, replacing it typically adds around $80 to $100 per sheet."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Permits: Most Utah municipalities require a building permit and inspection for a full roof replacement."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you can share your approximate square footage or the current material on your roof, I can help narrow down a more specific estimate for your project."
      }
    ],
